{"Working-hours bounds check computes both start and end from slotStartTime, never validating the slot end time against workingHour.endTime, incorrectly allowing slots that run past the end of working hours": 0.9689949750900269, "Two dayjs objects are compared using === (strict reference equality) which always returns false since each dayjs() call creates a new object, breaking detection of zero-length date overrides used to mark days as unavailable": 0.9683047533035278, "checkIfIsAvailable returns true immediately when a date override exists for the slot's day, skipping all busy-time overlap checks and allowing slots during actual conflicts, resulting in double-bookable slots": 0.9319115877151489, "getSlots calls .tz(override.timeZone) without guarding, but upstream producers of date overrides commonly provide only {start,end} without timeZone, causing potential runtime exceptions": 0.8178044557571411, "dateOverrides.find() returns truthy when it finds ANY override that the slot doesn't fit within, rather than checking if the slot is outside ALL overrides, incorrectly rejecting valid slots when multiple date overrides exist on the same day": 0.8880759477615356}